issue_body:
## Problem

`packages/surveys/src/lib/response-queue.ts` has three async calls dispatched as fire-and-forget without `.catch()` handlers. Each fails silently if IndexedDB rejects (quota exceeded, private-browsing quirks, transaction aborted, schema mismatch). Severity differs by site.

### Site 1 — line 120, `addPendingResponse` (highest severity)

```ts
if (this.config.persistOffline && this.config.surveyId) {
  void addPendingResponse({...}).then((dbId) => {
    if (dbId > 0) this.pendingDbIds.set(responseUpdate, dbId);
    this.processQueue();
  });
}
```

If `addPendingResponse` rejects: the `.then` callback never runs, `processQueue()` is never called, the response sits in the in-memory queue with no path forward, and the rejection leaks as unhandled. **The user sees no error but their response never gets sent.** This defeats the whole point of `persistOffline`.

### Site 2 — line 164, `syncPersistedResponses`

```ts
if (pendingCount > 1) {
  void this.syncPersistedResponses();
  return { success: false };
}
```

If sync throws: silent. The next `processQueue` call will re-attempt sync, so data isn't permanently lost — but every intermittent sync failure is invisible to telemetry, making debugging impossible.

### Site 3 — line 177, `removePendingResponse`

```ts
if (result.success) {
  const dbId = this.pendingDbIds.get(responseUpdate);
  if (dbId !== undefined) {
    void removePendingResponse(dbId);
    this.pendingDbIds.delete(responseUpdate);   // ← runs synchronously, unconditionally
  }
  ...
}
```

`this.pendingDbIds.delete(...)` runs synchronously. If the DB delete fails: in-memory state says "done," IndexedDB still has the row, next sync re-reads it and re-POSTs the same response. Depending on server-side dedup, either creates duplicates or leaves stale rows that fail to clear on every sync.

## Severity ranking

<!-- linear:table-colwidths:200,200,200 -->
| Site | Failure mode | Severity |
| -- | -- | -- |
| 1 | Silent response loss when persistOffline on | High |
| 3 | Duplicate POSTs or stale-row buildup | Medium |
| 2 | Lost telemetry on sync failures | Low |

## Fix the issue proposes vs. what's actually needed

Adding `.catch()` is necessary but not sufficient.

**Site 1** needs a `.catch()` that ALSO calls `processQueue()` — otherwise IndexedDB failure silently disables the entire submission path. Treat `persistOffline` as best-effort:

```ts
void addPendingResponse({...}).then((dbId) => {
  if (dbId > 0) this.pendingDbIds.set(responseUpdate, dbId);
  this.processQueue();
}).catch((err) => {
  logger.error({ err, surveyId: this.config.surveyId }, "Failed to persist pending response to IndexedDB");
  this.processQueue();   // ← fall through so the response isn't deadlocked
});
```

**Site 3** should defer `this.pendingDbIds.delete(responseUpdate)` until *after* the DB delete resolves, so in-memory and persistent state stay consistent. Otherwise just adding `.catch()` still leaves the duplicate-submission risk.

**Site 2** is fine with a plain `.catch(err => logger.error(...))`.

## External fix branch

[https://github.com/mirzasaikatahmmed/formbricks/tree/fix/surveys-validation-indexeddb-styles-test](<https://github.com/mirzasaikatahmmed/formbricks/tree/fix/surveys-validation-indexeddb-styles-test>)

### Issue Description

Hi,

When I try to upload a branding image inside the "Branding" section of my Organization on my self-hosted S3-compatible storage (GarageHQ), I receive the following error:

text
```
<Error>
  <Code>InvalidDigest</Code>
  <Message>Invalid digest: Failed to validate checksum for algorithm Crc32: calculated Some(Crc32([31, 18, 4, 43])), expected Crc32([0, 0, 0, 0])</Message>
  <Resource>/documenso-data/pa022by29gas/logo.png</Resource>
  <Region>garage</Region>
</Error>
```

Despite this error, document uploads complete successfully without issues.

Could you help to understand why this checksum validation error occurs during the image upload and how to resolve it?

Thank you in advance!


